  "id": "geometric-illusion",
  "term": "geometric illusion",
  "definition": "A geometric illusion is a visual misperception in which a simple geometric feature is seen differently because of the pattern around it. In the Müller-Lyer illusion, for example, the same line can look different in length depending on whether it ends with arrow tails or arrowheads.",
